  {
   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "A trader stores 500 quintals of tur dal in a public warehouse at ₹4 per quintal per month for 6 months. He pledges the warehouse receipt for a bank loan. (a) Find the storage charge. (b) Name the two functions of warehousing used."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "Storage charge = 500 × ₹4 × 6 = ₹12,000."
    },
    {
     "en": "Holding the dal for six months and releasing it later: stock piling (removes the hindrance of time)."
    },
    {
     "en": "Pledging the warehouse receipt for a loan: financing."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "₹12,000; stock piling and financing"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us work through this case together. A trader stores 500 quintals of tur dal in a public warehouse at ₹4 per quintal per month for 6 months. He pledges the warehouse receipt for a bank loan. (a) Find the storage charge. (b) Name the two functions of warehousing used."
   }
